# round 95 (w113): the cheapest recipe that respects one experiment and needs no solver at all. One growth ratio on the medium the labels come from, plus the six gene-protein-reaction redundancy counts, and nothing else on the logit. Every other metabolic arm either reads four media (four experiments) or needs a linear program per genotype. Reads fixed here: six seeds on the released split against the four-media counts-alone 0.902 and the one-medium ratio alone 0.877, and the five folds against the counts-alone 0.909 and the one-medium full recipe 0.932.
ESS_SOLVE_TABLE=/scratch/projects/torchcell-scratch/data/torchcell/reference_flux/ess_solve_encodings_YPD_gpronly.npz ESS_ARM=pooled ESS_HIDDEN=12 ESS_HEADS=4 ESS_LAYERS=1 ESS_PREPROC=1 ESS_EPOCHS=200 ESS_BATCH=32 ESS_POSW=1 ESS_SPLIT=ess_fcl_val0.2_s0.json.gz ESS_SEED=2703 ESS_TAG=_w113ypdgpronly ESS_OUT=w113_ypdgpronly_h12l1p1_e200_s2703 ESS_EXTRA='--node-embeddings pathways prot_T5_all --ess-readout fba --ess-fba-media YPD --ess-solve-features pfba --ess-solve-encoding log1p'
